  "term": "neuroethics",
  "definition": "Neuroethics is the area of ethics concerned with the ethical questions raised by neuroscience and neuroscientific innovations. It also becomes especially relevant where neuroscience overlaps with AI and neurotechnology in research, healthcare, and related applications.",
